  "question": {
    "text": "Which among the following statement(s) is (are) true for the extraction of aluminium from bauxite?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tJiCd",
      "text": "Hydrated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> precipitates, when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is bubbled through a solution of sodium aluminate.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ks3qW",
      "text": "Addition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math> lowers the melting point of alumina.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TsKl1",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is evolved at the anode during electrolysis.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZIfqJ",
      "text": "The cathode is a steel vessel with a lining of carbon.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NaAlO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>(B)&nbsp;In Hall-Heroult process&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>Al</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is mixed with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to lower melting point and&nbsp;increase conductivity.</p><p>(C)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Anode</mi><mtext>&#8196;C</mtext><mo>(</mo><mtext>s</mtext><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mtext>O</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mtext>melt</mtext><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mtext>CO</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mtext>g</mtext><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup></math></p><p>(D)&nbsp;Steel cathode with carbon lining and&nbsp;graphite anode are used.</p>",
